# hypernix.espresso_maker

4-tier evaluation: Ristretto / SingleShot / DoubleShot / Lungo — prompt battery + scoring.

## Documentation pages

- [EspressoMaker](../../#/docs/EspressoMaker) · [MDXL source](pages/EspressoMaker.mdxl)

## API reference

[Open the API reference source](pages/api-reference.mdxl)

### `EspressoMaker()`

Base espresso maker. Subclasses set sampling parameters.

### `EspressoMaker.pull(prompts, references=None) -> list[Shot]`

Generate ``samples_per_prompt`` samples per prompt, score

### `Ristretto()`

Shortest pull. Greedy decode, 16 tokens, single sample.

### `SingleShot()`

Standard pull. One sample, mild-temperature decode, 64 tokens.

### `DoubleShot()`

Two samples per prompt; the scorer picks the winner. Provide

### `Lungo()`

Long pull. Many samples, high temperature, 256 tokens. Good

### `espresso_maker(tier, oven, scorer=None, **kwargs) -> EspressoMaker`

Construct a tier by name.

